#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:2
msgid "add_custom_rule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:6
msgid "Add a custom template rule to the generated build system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:9
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:12
msgid ""
"`Generating Files`_\n"
"  add_custom_rule(<name> `OUTPUT`_ <output1> [<output2> ...]\n"
"                  COMMAND <command1> [<args1>...]\n"
"                  [...])\n"
"\n"
"`Derived Rule`_\n"
"  add_custom_rule(<name> `FROM_RULE`_ <rule>\n"
"                  [...])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:22
msgid "Generating Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:31
msgid "Add a custom template rule to produce an output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:33
msgid ""
"add_custom_rule(<name> OUTPUT <output1> [<output2> ...]\n"
"                       COMMAND <command1> [<args1>...]\n"
"                       [COMMAND <command2> [<args2>...]] ...\n"
"                       [DEPENDS <depends>...]\n"
"                       [BYPRODUCTS <files>...]\n"
"                       [DEPFILE <depfile>]\n"
"                       [CONFIGURATOR [FOR_FILE_SET <configurator>]\n"
"                                     [FOR_SOURCE <configurator>]]\n"
"                       [GLOBAL])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:45
msgid ""
"This defines a template rule ``<name>`` to generate specified ``OUTPUT`` "
"file(s). Rule names defined in all uppercase are reserved for CMake's own "
"built-in rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:49
msgid ""
"The association of source files with the template rule is done by creating :"
"ref:`file sets <File Sets>` of type ``<name>``. For each file of the file "
"set, a :command:`custom command <add_custom_command>` will be created in the "
"same directory as the target owning the file set and the output files of "
"this custom command will be declared as part of a file set attached to the "
"same target. The type of this file set, as well as its name, are controlled "
"by the :prop_rule:`OUTPUT_FILE_SET` rule property. This output file set will "
"have the same scope (``PRIVATE``, ``PUBLIC``, or ``INTERFACE``) as the input "
"file set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:59
msgid ""
"To parameterize the template, some patterns are defined which can be used as "
"part of the ``add_custom_rule`` arguments as well as the :ref:`rule's "
"properties <Rule Properties>`. These patterns will be instantiated for each "
"source file. The supported patterns are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:66
msgid ""
"The instantiation of the patterns are done in the context of the directory "
"where the file set was created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:69
msgid ""
"These patterns cannot be changed by the functions specified by the "
"``CONFIGURATOR`` option."
msgstr ""

