"`COMPILE_DEFINITIONS` file set property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:136
msgid ""
"For example, if the tool requires the flag ``-def:`` to identify a compile "
"definition, the following can be specified as part of the ``COMMAND`` option:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:140
msgid "$<LIST:TRANSFORM,<COMPILE_DEFINITIONS>,PREPEND,-def:>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:144
msgid "``<COMPILE_OPTIONS>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:145
msgid ""
"Content, in this order, of the :prop_rule:`COMPILE_OPTIONS` rule property, :"
"prop_sf:`COMPILE_OPTIONS` source property, and:prop_fs:`COMPILE_OPTIONS` "
"file set property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:149
msgid ""
"The options, which have the same semantics as those of the :command:"
"`add_custom_command` command, are:"
