#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:183
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:318
msgid "``FOR_FILE_SET``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:184
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:319
msgid ""
"The specified function will be called once per file set. The expected "
"signature is the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:190
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:207
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:325
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:338
msgid ""
"The arguments provide the names of the effective artifacts involved in the "
"current rule instantiation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:193
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:210
msgid ""
"The ``patterns`` argument holds the name of the variable which can be used "
"to enrich the list of patterns. The expected value is a :ref:`semicolon-"
"separated list <CMake Language Lists>` of  items having the syntax "
"``PATTERN=VALUE`` or ``PATTERN=``. More precisely, each item must match the "
"regular expression ``(^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+)=(.*)$``. Items which does not this "
"regular expression will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:200
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:331
msgid "``FOR_SOURCE``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:201
#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:332
msgid ""
"The specified function will be called for each file of the file set. The "
"expected signature is the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:219
msgid ""
"The source configurator is evaluated after the file set one. So, the changes "
"done by it will overwrite any changes done by the file set configurator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:225
msgid ""
"Any patterns specified through The :prop_fs:`RULE_PATTERNS` file set and :"
"prop_sf:`<RULE>_PATTERNS` source file properties will take precedence over, "
"respectively, the file set and the source configurators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/add_custom_rule.rst:229
